From 997c5cf2476bea6422e4cb79653b7cf2e23c57e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:23:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): book a run lost to its owner's unclean death as
 owner_restart_lost; systemic trips get a fix card [daveey]

One gateway segfault (David-MBP 10-30 12:26, pid 43117) made its in-flight managed runs exit 1 with
'service_identity_unverified'; three shared the fingerprint and the systemic rule parked them in sticky
triage with no owner.

- kanban_owner_death: owner-unavailable words + (unclean ledger record for the receipt's owner pid, or that
  pid gone) => owner_restart_lost, infrastructure, uncounted, respawn spaced by check_respawn_guard; the
  event names owner_death_pid. Crash-loop guard: a card also in flight at the owner's previous unclean
  death is charged normally (and never counted systemic).
- kanban_systemic_crash: a non-owner fingerprint seen >=3 times opens one fix card per fingerprint
  (idempotency key systemic-crash:<hash>, reused across ticks); tripped cards are linked as its children,
  carry fix_card in gave_up, and resume when it is done instead of a silent sticky hold.
